+## Delegated AlternativeStudy and verified projection seam (implementation draft)
+
+The delegated production `qmb optimize run` door accepts the existing exact CT47
+identifier envelope with command `optimize.run` and `mints_ct32=false`. Operator
+configuration selects exactly one Book, Alternative or AlternativeStudy private
+descriptor; incomplete, ambiguous or malformed descriptor presence refuses before
+compute. AlternativeStudy requires `operator-alternative-study-binding.json`,
+class `qmb-operator-alternative-study-binding-v1`, version 1, the complete existing
+Alternative binding, canonical Study settings and stable `study_fp1`. The plan is
+reconstructed through typed registered ports and pinned builder bytes. The outer
+descriptor hash is pinned before deriving invocation-specific `operational_fp1`.
+
+QMB owns trials, generation history, terminal artifacts and durable occurrence
+witnesses. Its seven-field Study result is retained without Book-only fields.
+Verify-only requires complete ordered history and the exact existing occurrence;
+it refuses incomplete history before running trials or writing a witness. Only
+the execution door can resume incomplete computation.
+
+Public projection v1 resolves an owned verified DONE Book result's declared
+`run_fp1`, independently reopens the original pinned CT32/CT29 lineage and returns
+the canonical saved-view body with a content fingerprint. The v1 public schema
+still exposes only `run_fp1` and optional `as_of`; QMA supplies canonical identity
+predicate `{"exclude":[]}`. The view is return-only and this read performs no
+artifact persistence, Experiment Ledger publication or environment occupancy.
+Study result readback is not a synthetic CT32 projection.
diff --git a/docs/components/qma-daemon.md b/docs/components/qma-daemon.md
