@@ -535,0 +536,29 @@
+
+## Authenticated Study execution and durable result readback (implementation draft)
+
+The existing `qmb.optimize.run` operation uses the same dispatched Task,
+AgentCapability admission, durable lease/attempt, host-observed deployment,
+ProductSession grant and environment checks as `qmb.backtest.run`. It passes its
+actual command to QMB and requires AlternativeStudy preflight. No additional
+human-only CT47 schema field, authority substitution or provider claim is needed.
+Task input validation runs after canonical grant validation and before consuming
+the place-run binding; current authority is also checked before worker acceptance.
+
+QMA keeps the seven-field Study terminal result in an immutable proof tied to its
+durable expected invocation. Authenticated `get_job` on an owned DONE QMB handle
+adds `verified_result` only after actual QMB verify-only reopening equals that
+proof. Original operator and originating ProductSession ownership remain required.
+Changed source bytes or incomplete/missing occurrence evidence refuse readback,
+including after daemon restart. QMA does not execute or manufacture missing trials.
+
+`qmb.analysis.project` read authority resolves one owned DONE Book source, verifies
+its exact stored result and asks QMB for a canonical saved view. The public v1
+`artifact_ref` is `{fp1,kind:"saved-view",body}` with fp1 of the body. It is an
+inline return value: query authority and publication authority remain separate.
+No QMA-side filter, compute, ledger append or publication occurs. Durable projection
+children use the same bounded 30-second deadline as terminal verification.
+
+Cancellation control files are isolated to each owned transport; a stale signal
+for the same opaque compiled job ID in another daemon cannot cancel a new run.
+Windows `qmb.exe` is subject to production preflight. Native containment refusals
+are unchanged.
